<http://data.silknow.org/object/ae378d9d-e23e-3195-bfe1-056764c46d2d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Knitted silk purse, with gilt opening bars and finger-ring"@en , "From the early eighteenth century, fine steel needles were used to knit purses and small bags in patterned silk, and their workmanship was very fine.  A small number of machine-knitted purses also began to become widely available.  This purse includes a finger ring."@en ;
