        ecrm:P3_has_note               "From the early eighteenth century, fine steel needles were used to knit purses and small bags in patterned silk, and their workmanship was very fine.  A small number of machine-knitted purses also began to become widely available.  This purse includes a finger ring."@en , "Knitted silk purse, with gilt opening bars and finger-ring"@en ;
